+        // [ff9mapkit netsync R3 s121] `netsync.menu_refusal` -- THE AUDIBLE MENU REFUSAL (guest side; NetSyncField.RefuseMainMenu, from
+        // UIKeyTrigger's Menu-key branch when the s38 gate refuses a mirroring guest): `now` (what a Menu press would do right now --
+        // "open" stock's main menu | "off" stock's own refusal, IsMenuControlEnable false | "audible" a mirroring guest on FieldHUD
+        // or WorldHUD: refused with SFX 102 and the line | "silent" a mirroring guest anywhere else, the diorama's BattleHUD among
+        // them: s38's silent drop | "dialog" the press takes UIKeyTrigger's DIALOGUE path -- a dialogue window up and not paused,
+        // or no scene for the UI state (NetSyncField.MenuKeyRoute) -- which s121 never sees: on a mirroring guest a silent drop
+        // counted NOWHERE, so a bench gates its press on `now` == "audible", not on ui_state FieldHUD; null = no UIManager),
+        // `count` (audible refusals), `lines` (of those, the ones that wrote "main menu suppressed (following guest) on field N",
+        // or "...on world map W" on WorldHUD -- a per-process latch per (class, place), never cleared at session end, so a second
+        // leg on the same field reads `lines` +0) and `silent` (silent drops) -- all three monotonic per process, read DELTAS --
+        // then the last refused press of either kind: `last_state` (its UIManager.UIState name; null = none yet), `last_field`
+        // (the place the line names: fldMapNo, or wldMapNo when `last_state` is WorldHUD; -1 = none yet), `age_ms` (since it; -1 =
+        // none yet) and `muted` (FF9Sfx.muteSfx at the last audible refusal: the buzz was asked for but the engine muted it).
+        // AppendNetsync's catch line carries the same keys at their sentinels.
+        private static void AppendMenuRefusal(StringBuilder sb)
+        {
+            sb.Append("\"menu_refusal\":{");
